WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
Two bright dates on a
timeline: 1912, and 1945.

2
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.250
Between them, a long, dark stretch.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.990
Out of the dark, shapes
rise one at a time.

4
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:13.990
A ship.

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.240
Two helmets.

6
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.810
A ballot box.

7
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:21.220
At one end, a small
stage, set in spring 1912.

8
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.610
At the other, an
audience, sitting in 1945.

9
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.880
Priestley wrote the play in 1944 and 1945.

10
00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.730
So why set it back in 1912?

11
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.890
In this mission, you'll map what
happened between those two dates.

12
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:41.190
You'll step into Britain in
1912: a rigid class system,

13
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.260
no welfare state, and no vote for women.

14
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:49.470
And you'll meet Britain in 1945,
the year of a Labour landslide.

15
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.460
Your mission: explain why Priestley
sets the play back in 1912.
